## 6. The data

### 6.1 The cue table

`VfxTable.Cues` and `VfxTable.Hits` are `CueTable<VfxDef>`: (owner, action) → the owner's
class → `any`, exactly as every director resolves (`Feedback.gdd` §2). A hit whose action
has no row falls to (`any`, `""`). Every row of the vocabulary (`Feedback.gdd` §6) has one —
the check asserts it:

| Cue | Effect | Medium | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|
| hit · `pomegraknight`/`ba`, `s2.seed` · `pumpking`/`ba.head`, `ba.explode` · *foe*/`contact` · `seagull`/`s2.dash` · unnamed | Hit spark by weight (+ hit react on the victim from Medium, + ground dust for contact) | attacker | Confirm |
| hit · `pomegraknight`/`s1.tornado` · `seagull`/`s1.poop` · `hazard`/`tsunami` | Hit spark in fire · in poison · a splash in water | attacker · attacker · arena | Confirm · Confirm · Critical |
| `spawn` (tag `born`) · `respawn` · `switch.in` / `switch.out` | Spawn pop (smaller) · bigger · closing / opening | body | Confirm |
| `jump` — ground · `air` · `swim` | Dust puff · a step-ring · bubbles | arena · body · arena | Cosmetic |
| `land` | Dust puff by impact speed (192–1100 px/s → 11–30 px) | arena | Cosmetic |
| `death` — any · fighter · boss | Death burst · big · big | body | Confirm · Critical · Critical |
| `heal` · `ult.ready` · `aggro` · `evolve` | Heal · Shine at the head · a small Shine above the head · Cast (a rising bloom) | body | Confirm · Critical · Confirm · Critical |
| `hurt.tick` — `hazard` / `burn` / `on_fire` / `frozen` | Sting in danger / fire / fire / ice | body | Confirm; **Critical on the player's side** |
| `hurt` (the Protect core) | Sting in the danger colour | arena | Critical |
| loop `status.burning` / `on_fire` / `frozen` / `trapped` / `stunned` | Status loop | body | Critical |
| loop `telegraph` | Telegraph on the real reach, danger colour | body | Critical |
| `pomegraknight` / `ba.swing` · `s1.cast` · loop `s1.tornado` · `s1.tornado.tick` · `s2.cast` · `s2.wave` · `s2.seed.expire` | Slash arc · Cast · Field loop · Ring · Cast · Trail · Expire pop | hers | Confirm; the field Critical; the expire Cosmetic |
| `ba.explode` (tag `dud`) | Burst to the blast radius (an Expire pop) | owner | Critical (Confirm) |
| `world` / `soft.enter`, `soft.exit` — `water` · `foliage` · `cloud` · `kit` · other | Splash · Rustle · Dust puff · Rustle · Rustle | arena | Cosmetic |
| `hazard` / `tick` — `fire` · `freeze` · `lava` · `spike` · `poop` · `damage` | Sting (lava: an Expire pop; spike: a Hit spark) | arena | Confirm; Critical on the player's side |
| `flow` / `arena.enter` | The realm's ambience starts; pools warm | arena | — |
| `flow` / `countdown.tick` · `countdown.go` · `mission.start` | A closing ring · Shine · a ring | arena | Confirm · Critical · Cosmetic |
| `flow` / `mission.success` · `mission.fail` · `boss.intro` · `boss.defeated` · `player.down` · `run.over` (`victory`) | Cast · a smoke puff · Shine in danger · a Burst · a danger ring · smoke (Shine) | arena | Critical (run.over: Cosmetic) |

### 6.2 A row (`VfxDef`)

`Id` · `Archetype` · whose medium (`Style`, else `StyleFrom`) · colours (`OwnerColours`, else
`Element`) · the size rule (`SizeFrom`: fixed px, the cue's reach, its box, its magnitude
mapped to a range, the body's radius, or the hit's weight) · `Variants` (a shuffle-bag) ·
jitter ranges (`RotJitterDeg`, `ScaleJitter`, `TimeJitter`, `HueJitter` — how far the main
colour may lean to its second) · `Count`, `Life` · `Priority` (+ `CriticalForPlayer`) ·
`Cooldown` (per source) · `MinMagnitude` · `Follow`, `Anchor` · `FlourishOneIn` ·
`Modifiers` · `Layers` (more rows on the same cue) · `ByTag` (the row the cue's tag selects).

Hit marks, by weight (radius, before the victim's radius factor 0.85–1.6):
Graze 4 · Light 7 · Medium 11 · Heavy 16 · Massive 23 px — a fighter is 64 px tall.

### 6.3 State and pace

A `VfxModifier` applies when **all** its conditions hold: the source body's `FeedbackState`
(any of the flags), the cue's `Tag`, `MinCombo`, `MinIntensity`, `MinBossPhase`, `Killed`,
`MinWeight`, `Stage`. It multiplies count, scale, life and speed, may repaint the effect in
another element, set flags, or add a layer.

| In use | When | Then |
|---|---|---|
| burning swing | tag `burning` | repaint in fire, flame motes join |
| attacker on fire | state `Burning` on the attacker | a fire lick is added to the hit |
| under water | state `Submerged` | dust becomes bubbles |
| a kill | `Killed` | pieces ×1.5, size ×1.15 |
| combo | `MinCombo` 4 | size ×1.06 |
| boss enraged | `MinBossPhase` 2 | size ×1.12, pieces ×1.25 (hits and telegraphs) |
| frozen victim | state `Frozen` on the victim | its reaction is ice |

The **blackboard** the director keeps (`VfxDirector`): `Intensity` 0–1 (+0.07 a hit, +0.012 a
cue, half-life 1.6 s), `Combo` (the player's side's hits within 1.4 s of each other),
`BossPhase` (0 none · 1 after `boss.intro` · 2 once the boss reports low health · 0 at
`boss.defeated`). Built in: every third hit of a combo is one step of escalation, up to
three (+7 % size, +18 % pieces a step); at intensity ≥ 0.70 decoration thins (pieces ×0.6,
life ×0.85) so a crowded fight stays readable.

### 6.4 No fatigue

Shape variants from a shuffle-bag (every variant once before a repeat, never the same twice
across a refill) · jitter inside the row's ranges · context (burning, kill, weight, combo,
boss phase, the canvas) · a one-in-twenty glint on named hits · a graze is a fleck and
nothing else · a stream of effects is thinned by the per-frame cap and by intensity.

---

## 7. Budget

Our own targets — no external numbers exist for 2D [R2 B8.5]. `VfxBudget`:

| Budget | Cap | Measured (three staged fights, real renderer) |
|---|---|---|
| Drawn marks alive | 72 pooled (Cosmetic stops at 36, Confirm at 56) | peak 13–19 |
| One-shot emitters alive | 24 pooled (10 / 18) | peak 9–13 |
| Particles alive, ambience included | 512 (220 / 400); ≤ 32 a burst | peak 49–97 |
| Ambient emitters · particles | 2 · ≤ 24 a realm | 8–24 |
| Loops alive | 24 | ≤ 4 |
| Effects started per frame (not Critical) | 6 | — |
| Texture memory | 16 generated textures, ≤ 64 px a side | 63 KB in all |
| Garbage | 0 bytes per cue, per frame and per draw | 0 (§10) |

- **Three priorities.** *Critical* (telegraphs, status loops, fields, the player's own
  hurt, a fighter's death, blasts, the big flow beats) is never refused: with the pool full
  it takes the oldest lesser mark. *Confirm* (hit sparks, spawns) is refused over its
  threshold. *Cosmetic* (dust, splashes, rustles, reactions) goes first.
- **Off screen**, nothing but Critical is started (160 px margin).
- **`FeedbackSettings.Particles`** (0.25–1) scales the piece counts of everything that is
  not Critical, and the ambience; it never removes an effect.
- A mark is **one canvas command** (a triangle mesh with per-vertex colour) and is redrawn
  only when its medium's frame changes; a mark that follows a body is moved, not redrawn.
- In the staged fights 14–40 Confirm and 4–16 Cosmetic effects were refused each — foes
  spawning off screen, and seed hits landing more than six to a frame. No Critical was.
- Whole-scene draw calls stayed 27–40 a frame with effects running.

---

## 8. Authored art replaces procedural

Two levels, same contract as a tile — keep the name and the footprint (`RealmStyleBible` §1):

1. **A texture.** `res://Assets/Vfx/<id>.png` replaces the generated texture of that id
   (`watercolour/drop`, `ink/drybrush`, `realism/spark`, `gongbi/bubble` … —
   `VfxTextures.All`). Same size, same orientation (a particle's leading end is down).
2. **A whole effect.** `res://Assets/Vfx/<style>/<effect id>.png` — a horizontal strip of
   square frames — replaces the procedural effect of that row in that medium
   (`Assets/Vfx/watercolour/pome_slash.png`). It is played on a pooled mark at the medium's
   own frame rate (24 fps at most), sized by the row's size rule (the strip's frame is
   2 × size across) and turned to the cue's direction. Nothing else changes: the row, the
   budget, the modifiers still apply.

Neither needs a code change; `Assets/Vfx/` does not exist yet.

---

## 9. Deferred, and what is missing

| Deferred | Why |
|---|---|
| Watching it move | Stills were judged; tempo and density at play speed were not (§11) |
| The four other kits' own abilities | Out of scope; their cues are not raised yet. Until then every hit they land is drawn as the generic hit of their home medium, and the attacker is *inferred* (the player, when a foe is hit) |
| Decals (juice stains, poop splats), trails on projectiles, afterimages | Pooled decals and ≤ 8 trails are budgeted in R2 §4.9 but not built |
| A cue for a status **ending** with a flourish (Blush's steam puff, a thaw's shatter) | The loop's stop is told; nothing says *how* it ended |
| `arena.enter` from the map editor's Playtest | The Playtest raises none, so its effects use the default medium. (Zone 6 raises its variant's tag since v0.12.0 — §4) |
| The fan's real angles on `s2.wave`; the swing's cone for the other kits | `CueShapes.Cone` is there to be used when they are wired |
| Screen-space distortion, glow, 2D lights, `CanvasGroup` outlines | Cost on the Mobile renderer unmeasured [R2 B9.19, *from memory*] |
| A spawn queue ("wait two frames, then drop") | Over-budget effects are dropped at once; simpler, and nothing Critical is affected |
| `GPUParticles2D` | Not used: at ≤ 32 particles a burst and ≤ 24 of ambience it did not earn its place |
| An options screen; quality tiers | `FeedbackSettings.Particles` is read; nothing writes it |
| Audio | The same vocabulary; another team |

---

## 10. Verification

- **Headless:** `Godot --headless --path . res://Scenes/Feedback/VfxCheck.tscn` — `40-QA.md`.
  1 298 checks in 12 s: every vocabulary row resolves for every owner and class and plays
  in all ten media; pools are reused and return clean; budgets hold under a flood; loops
  stop when stopped and when their source leaves; nothing survives an arena; the settings
  scale; allocation is zero. Mutation-tested: twenty deliberate breakages, twenty failed by
  name. Its measured lines:

```
vfx  tables       10 media · 79 rows (43 cue keys, 10 hit keys) · 16 textures, 63.3 KB
vfx  coverage     380 vocabulary rows resolve (every owner × every class) · 750 of them played in 10 media: 3319 marks drawn, 0 draw errors
vfx  whose medium a slash is the attacker's (watercolour in an ink arena) · dust the arena's · an unwired kit its home medium's · the slash on 130 px / 40.0°, the field on 128 × 40, the blast to 96 px, the tell along 480 px
vfx  pools        98 nodes for the whole game (72 marks, 24 emitters, 2 ambient) · 121 mark rents in 40 rounds, 0 created, all returned clean
vfx  budget       a flood of 3 660 cues over 30 frames: peak 72/72 marks, 18/24 emitters, 106/512 particles · refused 1540 Confirm, 3081 Cosmetic, 0 Critical · 37 marks handed to Critical effects · 30 status loops asked, 24 run
vfx  the arena    Wulin: ink, a pale canvas, 2 ambient emitters / 12 particles · everything gone when the arena left · pool unchanged at 98 nodes
vfx  settings     Particles 1 → 0.25: a massive hit's pieces 18 → 5, its marks 2 → 2, a Critical blast 14 → 14, ambience 12 → 3 · variety: 3 shapes, 0 repeats in 400, 26 flourishes
vfx  allocation   18000 cues raised with the director acting on each: 0 bytes · 120 frames of its update: 0 bytes · 1572 mark draws: 0 bytes · worst medium to draw: 0 bytes
```
- **By eye:** `Scenes/Dev/VfxGallery.tscn` (needs a window, scratch `HOME`) — the archetype
  × style grid on a dark and a pale backdrop, the protagonists' looks, a hit and a slash at
  five moments of their lives, each realm's air, and a staged fight in the real Arena on a
  mid-tone, a pale and a dark map. Eight captures are kept in `Docs/Art/Vfx/captures/`.

---

## 11. What looking at it changed

Four passes in the real renderer (2026-11-26). Each line is something no check could find.

| Seen | Change |
|---|---|
| Every slash was a bulging half-moon, its tips short of the cone | The crescent's centre line bends inward so its **outer edge is the arc of the reach** and it ends in points |
| Stepped media showed nothing for their first frame (83–100 ms late) | A stepped mark shows the *middle* of each held frame |
| The same four-point cross in every "pop" read as a targeting reticle | A kill, a spawn and a shine no longer share it; a watercolour glint is a soft sparkle, not an inked cross |
| Hit marks buried the fighter they landed on | Sizes roughly halved (§6.2); the wash thinned |
| The Fire Tornado was a rectangle with a helix in it | Soft media draw a field as ribbons that reach the box's edges; only hard media show the box |
| Ink and watercolour on a dark canvas wore a white sticker | Their paper is now a soft, quarter-strength breath under the mark |
| Scratchboard and pixel slashes were a single thin line | Scratched in over two frames, six lines; pixel strokes as thick as their crescent |
| Ambience could not be seen | Every realm's motes ×1.6 (`VfxTable.AmbientScale`) |
| **The player vanished on the frame she was hit** | The i-frame blink opened on its "off" half and hid the body — and the flash — for the first ~20 ms. The blink now waits for the flash (`CharacterController`, one line) |

**The hit flash** (`Feedback.gdd` §5.3), seen for the first time: on foes it is a clean
silhouette that keeps the sprite's shape — **white** on the beach (mid) and in the Dungeon
(dark), **ink** on Wulin's paper (pale) — and reads at once on all three. On the player it
is the same once the blink fix is in. **The camera:** a Light hit reads 0.21–0.26 trauma
(≈ 1.5–2 px, gone in 70 ms at `Decay` 3 /s) — carried by the 2 px kick, as designed; the
third slash 0.41; a kill 0.33–0.63; the player hit 0.38 with a 4–10 px kick away from the
blow and a 1.006 zoom. Stills cannot show whether that *feels* right.

**Still wrong, in my eye:** status loops are small and timid; the realism smoke is thin;
the pixel hit's plus frame dominates its four; watercolour on a dark canvas goes chalky;
the gallery's telegraph cannot show its fill; ambience is still sparse on big screens.

---

## 12. Decisions log

| Date | Decision | Why |
|---|---|---|
| 2026-11-26 | An effect = an archetype rendered by a style; one style per medium | The brief; adding a world is adding a style |
| 2026-11-26 | A style is five primitives; the base class composes everything else | Ten media × twenty archetypes would otherwise be two hundred hand-written effects |
| 2026-11-26 | Drawn marks are one triangle mesh each, built in static buffers and sent straight to the rendering server | One canvas command, per-vertex colour for soft edges without textures, no allocation |
| 2026-11-26 | Emitters for continuous media, drawn stepped pieces for stamped media | A particle node cannot snap to a grid or turn in 45° steps |
| 2026-11-26 | `CPUParticles2D` for bursts **and** ambience; no `GPUParticles2D` | Counts are tiny; no restart latency, no process material [R2 B9, verified] |
| 2026-11-26 | Pooled nodes are the director's own children and live for the whole session | No scene owns them; nothing to leak on a scene change |
| 2026-11-26 | Dust belongs to the ground (the arena's medium); an air jump's ring to the body | Reconciles "a body's own effects" with "dust on the ground" |
| 2026-11-26 | The contrast guard is three canvases, and each medium brings its own ground | A bool was not enough: the beach is neither pale nor dark |
| 2026-11-26 | Hit marks are 4–23 px | Looked at; twice that hid fighters |
| 2026-11-26 | `ba.swing` carries its cone in `Extents` (`CueShapes.Cone`) rather than a new `Cue` field | The contract's five types stay as they are while the audio team builds on them |
| 2026-11-26 | `arena.enter` carries the arena as its `Source`; the director ends ambience when that node leaves the tree | A loop whose source leaves is ended by listeners already; no new cue |
| 2026-11-26 | The i-frame blink waits for the hit flash | Found in the captures; visual only |
| 2026-11-26 | **For the owner:** Cleopastar → poster and Sifu Pangda → ink remain provisional; the VOID style has no bible; Cloud Court (`CC`) keeps the enamel style though no world owns it | One field each in `VfxTable.Looks` |

**v0.12.0 (zone 6).** Two arena tags (`void_frontier`, `avici`) map to the VOID medium, and the
Unwritten's **Styx Tide** has a hit row of its own — `hazard`/`styx_tide`, a splash in the
arena's medium like the tsunami's (`VfxTable`). The wave itself is drawn by its hazard until it
has art (a Prussian-blue wall with a white crest — the Void Frontier's cyanotype).
